# ============================================================
# MODULE 07 — EXPERIMENTATION & EVALUATION
# Urban Mobility Intelligence & Multi-Agent Traffic Control
# ============================================================
#
# Purpose:
#   Benchmark traffic-signal control strategies in SUMO using
#   consistent network-level traffic metrics.
#
# Policies evaluated:
#   1. Fixed-time baseline
#   2. Cyclic phase-control baseline
#   3. Decentralized multi-agent queue-based heuristic
#
# Evaluation metrics:
#   - Average queue
#   - Maximum queue
#   - Average waiting time
#   - Maximum waiting time
#   - Average vehicles
#   - Peak vehicles
#
# Experimental setup:
#   - SUMO
#   - 2 x 2 intersection grid
#   - 1000 simulation steps
#   - Random seed = 42
#   - Decision interval = 10 simulation steps
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   The multi-agent policy is a heuristic controller.
#   It is NOT a trained MARL/PPO policy.
#
# Research role:
#   Provides a reproducible benchmark for comparing the current
#   control strategies before introducing learned MARL policies.
#
# ============================================================


# ============================================================
# 1. IMPORTS & CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================

